---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="LLM Vendor Partnership — Value Proposal"
  description="What the Poesis stack brings to LLM capabilities — and what LLMs bring to Poesis. Models propose; humans dispose through ITIP; SIE evaluates constraints and executes governed Mechanisms."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Partnerships</p>
      <h1>LLM Vendor Partnership — Value Proposal</h1>
      <p class="lead"><strong>Better context beats bigger models.</strong> Frontier models reason against statistical traces of the world — not against an explicit, causal, governed model of the world. That single gap drives both of today's ceilings: the <a href="#partnership-thesis"><strong>capability ceiling</strong> and the <strong>deployment ceiling</strong></a>. Poesis closes both through a systemic model of the world named <i>Generative System Model</i>, implemented by SIE, and surfaced through domain platforms such as ITIP — and model vendors are the natural partners on it.</p>
      <div class="reference-disclosure">
        <strong>How to read this proposal.</strong> Present tense describes the Poesis reference design and target operating model which might not yet be fully implemented or operational. Partnership adherences described below may therefore include work to advance Poesis components from their explicitly stated maturity levels.
      </div>
      <div class="hero-cta">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact">Talk to us</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/gsm">The GSM standard</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/sie">The SIE engine</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--soft" id="partnership-thesis">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">The partnership thesis</p>
      <h2>Five reasons to partner.</h2>
      <p class="lead">One partnership addresses two limits: structured context raises the <strong>capability ceiling</strong>; enterprise platform, market access, platform advantage, and sovereignty raise the <strong>deployment ceiling</strong>.</p>
      <div class="thesis-grid">
        <div class="card card--feature" id="capability-ceiling">
          <span class="tag">Capability ceiling · Structured context</span>
          <h3>Better intelligence without bigger models.</h3>
          <p>A model that trains and reasons against explicit, causal, governed, and snapshot Definitions of the world works against explicit structure rather than relying only on correlation. That structure provides a substrate for impact analysis, counterfactual testing, and planning against modeled dependencies and much more...</p>
          <p class="thesis-mechanisms"><strong>Supported by adherences</strong> B · Governed inference grounding + D · Model specialisation + E · Model evaluation and assurance</p>
          <p class="thesis-tagline">Don't compete on larger models. Compete on better intelligence.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card card--feature" id="deployment-ceiling">
          <span class="tag">Deployment ceiling · Enterprise platform</span>
          <h3>From language model to enterprise AI platform.</h3>
          <p>Companies buy solutions, not models. Partner models provide the intelligence; Poesis provides structured organizational context, human loop, deterministic evaluation of inference, grounded enterprise agentic development workflows, and audit evidence for accountability. Together they form a deployable enterprise agentic platform — able to act, not only answer.</p>
          <p class="thesis-mechanisms"><strong>Supported by adherences</strong> B · Governed inference grounding + C · Governed inference deployment + F · Model qualification and routing</p>
          <p class="thesis-tagline">Transform a model into an enterprise AI platform.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card card--feature">
          <span class="tag">Deployment ceiling · Market access</span>
          <h3>A credible path into regulated industries.</h3>
          <p>Enterprises don't stall because AI isn't powerful enough — they stall because they can't trust it to act. Explainability, governance, auditability, and policy enforcement are entry conditions, and Poesis is designed to provide their shared context and control substrate.</p>
          <p class="thesis-mechanisms"><strong>Supported by adherences</strong> C · Governed inference deployment + E · Model evaluation and assurance</p>
          <p class="thesis-tagline">Governance is the entry ticket to regulated industries.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card card--feature">
          <span class="tag">Deployment ceiling · Platform advantage</span>
          <h3>A defensible advantage beyond model performance.</h3>
          <p>Grounded inference, governed execution, and model specialisation create a combined platform that is harder to commoditize than standalone inference. It moves the commercial relationship into AI governance, digital operating models, enterprise transformation, and regulated automation — increasing deal scope and strategic relevance.</p>
          <p class="thesis-mechanisms"><strong>Supported by adherences</strong> B · Governed inference grounding + C · Governed inference deployment + D · Model specialisation + E · Model evaluation and assurance + F · Model qualification and routing</p>
          <p class="thesis-tagline">Build a platform advantage, not simply a model advantage.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card card--feature">
          <span class="tag">Deployment ceiling · Sovereignty</span>
          <h3>The foundation of a sovereign AI stack.</h3>
          <p>Not "a sovereign LLM" — a sovereign AI <em>stack</em>. You provide the sovereign intelligence. Poesis provides the governed context. Together they form the trusted infrastructure enterprises need to deploy AI at scale. <strong>As a neutral, model-independent substrate, GSM/SIE could be advanced as a candidate foundation for future European standardization of governed enterprise AI.</strong></p>
          <p class="thesis-mechanisms"><strong>Supported by adherences</strong> A–G · The complete governed AI value cycle</p>
          <p class="thesis-tagline">Build the sovereign AI stack, not only a sovereign model.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">The value mechanisms / adherences</p>
      <h2>How the partnership creates value.</h2>
      <p class="lead">An adherence is a concrete interface where partner capabilities and Poesis components combine to create reciprocal value. Each business outcome is supported by one or more such mechanisms.</p>
      <div class="value-grid">
        <button class="card value-card" data-flow="A" type="button" aria-pressed="false" aria-controls="vf-detail">
          <span class="tag">A · Structured context sourcing</span>
          <h3>Definitions sourced at scale</h3>
          <p>Partner models are designed to become KnowledgeSources over code repositories and, through additional adapters, other authoritative resources — broadening sourcing while preserving human disposition.</p>
          <span class="value-link">View flow details</span>
        </button>
        <button class="card value-card" data-flow="B" type="button" aria-pressed="false" aria-controls="vf-detail">
          <span class="tag">B · Augmented inference</span>
          <h3>Governed causal grounding</h3>
          <p>SIE can expose systematically sourced governed Definitions of the organization through a model-facing context and tool surface, enabling inference against explicit structure (causal, temporal, logical, semantic, evaluable) rather than prose documents alone.</p>
          <span class="value-link">View flow details</span>
        </button>
        <button class="card value-card" data-flow="C" type="button" aria-pressed="false" aria-controls="vf-detail">
          <span class="tag">C · Governed inference</span>
          <h3>Governed action in regulated estates</h3>
          <p>Models propose; SIE operates governance rules and evaluations deterministically; humans dispose throught domain application. The target result is accountable, traceable action.</p>
          <span class="value-link">View flow details</span>
        </button>
        <button class="card value-card" data-flow="D" type="button" aria-pressed="false" aria-controls="vf-detail">
          <span class="tag">D · Model specialisation</span>
          <h3>A governed specialisation substrate</h3>
          <p>Governed Definitions and Ascription history could provide typed domain material for controlled adaptation. Corpus construction, source provenance, rights enforcement, training integration, and measured uplift remain research work.</p>
          <span class="value-link">View flow details</span>
        </button>
        <button class="card value-card" data-flow="E" type="button" aria-pressed="false" aria-controls="vf-detail">
          <span class="tag">E · Model evaluation and assurance</span>
          <h3>Governed evidence of model capability</h3>
          <p>GSM contracts and SIE Mechanisms can turn defined enterprise tasks into reproducible evaluations, revealing model capability, failure boundaries, and regressions without requiring weight adaptation.</p>
          <span class="value-link">View flow details</span>
        </button>
        <button class="card value-card" data-flow="F" type="button" aria-pressed="false" aria-controls="vf-detail">
          <span class="tag">F · Model qualification and routing</span>
          <h3>The right model for each governed workload</h3>
          <p>A vendor-neutral catalog and routing contract can qualify models against workload needs, cost, and measured outcomes — creating evidence-based placement rather than one-model-fits-all selection.</p>
          <span class="value-link">View flow details</span>
        </button>
        <button class="card value-card" data-flow="G" type="button" aria-pressed="false" aria-controls="vf-detail">
          <span class="tag">G · Agentic delivery</span>
          <h3>A governed agentic delivery proof</h3>
          <p>Partner models power specialist agents under declared workflows; the deterministic harness enforces artifact, authorization, and workflow gates and record comparable delivery evidence.</p>
          <span class="value-link">View flow details</span>
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--soft" id="value-map">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">The value flows</p>
      <h2>An interactive map of the exchange.</h2>

      <div id="vf">
        <div class="vf-notices" role="region" aria-label="How to read the value map">
          <p class="vf-notice vf-notice-info"><strong>Explore the map.</strong> Click a flow to see its mutual value. Click an LLM or Poesis component to see every adherence it has with the other components. Expand a Poesis box for internal detail.</p>
          <p class="vf-notice vf-notice-invariant"><strong>Core invariant:</strong> models <strong>PROPOSE</strong> (inferred, confidence &lt; 1.0) · accountable humans dispose through ITIP · SIE evaluates constraints and executes governed Mechanisms — <strong>PROPOSE / DISPOSE</strong>.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="vf-human">
          <strong>By design, human supervision, regulation, and governance remain in the loops.</strong>
          <ul>
            <li><b>Owns Intents</b> — creation of Definitions / Ascriptions.</li>
            <li><b>Owns Approvals</b> — validation of AI-proposed Definitions / Ascriptions.</li>
            <li><b>Owns Accountability</b> — evaluation and simulation of Definition / Ascription compliance and impacts, and audit of AI and human actions over Definitions / Ascriptions.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="vf-diagram" id="vf-diagram">
          <svg id="vf-wires" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"></svg>
          <div class="vf-cols">

            <div class="vf-col">
              <div class="vf-group" id="g-partner">
                <div class="vf-gtitle">LLM operations</div>
                <div class="vf-gsub">vendor-neutral by design — any sovereign or frontier model: self-hosted, sovereign-hosted, or open-weight</div>

                <div class="vf-card" id="n-train" data-component="Model adaptation &amp; specialisation">
                  <button class="vf-card-select" type="button" aria-pressed="false" aria-controls="vf-detail">
                    <span class="vf-ctitle">Model adaptation &amp; specialisation</span>
                    <span class="vf-csub">adapts through governed context, structured supervision, and evaluation signals — under explicit rights controls</span>
                  </button>
                </div>

                <div class="vf-card" id="n-infer" data-component="Grounded inference">
                  <button class="vf-card-select" type="button" aria-pressed="false" aria-controls="vf-detail">
                    <span class="vf-ctitle">Grounded inference</span>
                    <span class="vf-csub">reasons against governed Definitions that model causal structure and carry traceable provenance — explicit context beyond document-only retrieval</span>
                  </button>
                </div>

                <div class="vf-card" id="n-eval" data-component="Model evaluation &amp; qualification">
                  <button class="vf-card-select" type="button" aria-pressed="false" aria-controls="vf-detail">
                    <span class="vf-ctitle">Model evaluation &amp; qualification</span>
                    <span class="vf-csub">submits versioned model outputs and configurations for governed evaluation, comparison, and workload qualification</span>
                  </button>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="vf-gutter"></div>

            <div class="vf-col">
              <div class="vf-group" id="g-poesis">
                <div class="vf-gtitle">Poesis stack</div>
                <div class="vf-gsub">one sovereign instance per organisation — tenant-owned, designed for future federation</div>

                <div class="vf-card" id="n-sie" data-component="SIE — Systemic Intelligence Engine">
                  <button class="vf-card-select" type="button" aria-pressed="false" aria-controls="vf-detail">
                    <span class="vf-ctitle">SIE — Systemic Intelligence Engine</span>
                    <span class="vf-csub">reference implementation of GSM containing Definitions / Ascriptions of the organisation and implementing their governance lifecycle</span>
                  </button>
                  <button class="vf-fold-btn" type="button" data-fold="f-sie" aria-controls="f-sie" aria-expanded="false">▸ components</button>
                  <div class="vf-fold" id="f-sie" hidden>
                    <div class="vf-comp"><b>sie-definition-manager</b> — hosts GSM, Ascription lifecycle, governance grammar</div>
                    <div class="vf-comp"><b>sie-definition-blackboard-manager</b> — contribution registry and Blackboard-seal lifecycle</div>
                    <div class="vf-comp"><b>sie-operator</b> — executes in-effect Mechanisms and validates typed inputs and effects; automatic Norm preflight remains to be built</div>
                  </div>
                </div>

                <div class="vf-card vf-gate" id="n-itip" data-component="ITIP — domain platform (IT)">
                  <button class="vf-card-select" type="button" aria-pressed="false" aria-controls="vf-detail">
                    <span class="vf-ctitle">ITIP — domain platform (IT)</span>
                    <span class="vf-csub">target domain surface for the <b>PROPOSE / DISPOSE gate to humans</b> — intent, approval, audit, and simulation</span>
                  </button>
                  <button class="vf-fold-btn" type="button" data-fold="f-itip" aria-controls="f-itip" aria-expanded="false">▸ components</button>
                  <div class="vf-fold" id="f-itip" hidden>
                    <div class="vf-comp"><b>itip-web-application</b> — planned human gate for intent, approval, simulation, appraisal, and audit</div>
                    <div class="vf-comp"><b>itip-frameworks</b> — source GDPR, NIS2, DORA, AI Act, TOGAF, ISO, and other domain vocabulary into GSM Definitions</div>
                    <div class="vf-comp"><b>itip-definition-blackboard-*-sourcer</b> — designed to wrap LLMs / agents as KnowledgeSources over code repositories; other source classes require adapters</div>
                  </div>
                </div>

                <div class="vf-card" id="n-saf" data-component="SAFe Agentic Framework">
                  <button class="vf-card-select" type="button" aria-pressed="false" aria-controls="vf-detail">
                    <span class="vf-ctitle">SAFe Agentic Framework</span>
                    <span class="vf-csub">agentic organisation product delivery through declared workflows today, with a deterministic operational harness specified</span>
                  </button>
                  <button class="vf-fold-btn" type="button" data-fold="f-saf" aria-controls="f-saf" aria-expanded="false">▸ components</button>
                  <div class="vf-fold" id="f-saf" hidden>
                    <div class="vf-comp"><b>orchestrator-agent</b> — portfolio / program / team</div>
                    <div class="vf-comp"><b>specialist-agent</b> — architecture, dev, QA, security, docs agents</div>
                    <div class="vf-comp"><b>harness</b> — specified deterministic FSM, artifact, authorization, and gate checks; runtime implementation remains</div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="vf-mobile-flows" role="group" aria-label="Selectable value relationships">
            <button class="vf-mobile-flow" type="button" data-flow="A" aria-pressed="false" aria-controls="vf-detail">
              <span class="vf-mobile-flow-code">A · Context sourcing</span>
              <strong>Sovereign LLM partner → Poesis stack</strong>
              <span>LLM-backed sourcing of GSM</span>
            </button>
            <button class="vf-mobile-flow" type="button" data-flow="B" aria-pressed="false" aria-controls="vf-detail">
              <span class="vf-mobile-flow-code">B · Governed inference grounding</span>
              <strong>Poesis stack → Sovereign LLM partner</strong>
              <span>Governed causal context + tools</span>
            </button>
            <button class="vf-mobile-flow" type="button" data-flow="C" aria-pressed="false" aria-controls="vf-detail">
              <span class="vf-mobile-flow-code">C · Governed inference deployment</span>
              <strong>Sovereign LLM partner → Poesis stack</strong>
              <span>Proposals → human disposition</span>
            </button>
            <button class="vf-mobile-flow" type="button" data-flow="D" aria-pressed="false" aria-controls="vf-detail">
              <span class="vf-mobile-flow-code">D · Model specialisation</span>
              <strong>Poesis stack → Sovereign LLM partner</strong>
              <span>Governed material for model adaptation</span>
            </button>
            <button class="vf-mobile-flow" type="button" data-flow="E" aria-pressed="false" aria-controls="vf-detail">
              <span class="vf-mobile-flow-code">E · Model evaluation and assurance</span>
              <strong>Poesis stack ↔ Sovereign LLM partner</strong>
              <span>Governed tests → comparable evidence</span>
            </button>
            <button class="vf-mobile-flow" type="button" data-flow="F" aria-pressed="false" aria-controls="vf-detail">
              <span class="vf-mobile-flow-code">F · Model qualification and routing</span>
              <strong>Poesis stack → Sovereign LLM partner</strong>
              <span>Workload demand → qualified model placement</span>
            </button>
            <button class="vf-mobile-flow" type="button" data-flow="G" aria-pressed="false" aria-controls="vf-detail">
              <span class="vf-mobile-flow-code">G · Agentic delivery</span>
              <strong>Sovereign LLM partner → Poesis stack</strong>
              <span>Agent bench builds the stack</span>
            </button>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="vf-detail" id="vf-detail" role="region" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="false" tabindex="-1" hidden></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="maturity">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="maturity-panel">
        <p class="eyebrow">Maturity disclosure</p>
        <h2>Operational maturity by value flow.</h2>
        <p>Current maturity and partnership work are stated separately for each flow. Implementation is part of the exchange: a partner can contribute model access, engineering, evaluation, and applied research to turn selected flows into measured operational proofs.</p>
        <div class="maturity-grid">
          <article>
            <span class="maturity-flow">Context sourcing</span>
            <strong class="maturity-status">Current maturity · Implemented substrate, designed client</strong>
            <p><strong>Partnership work:</strong> implement KnowledgeSources, model integration, client reduction, provenance transfer, and Definition Manager registration.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span class="maturity-flow">Governed inference grounding</span>
            <strong class="maturity-status">Current maturity · Implemented semantic and execution foundations</strong>
            <p><strong>Partnership work:</strong> build the model-facing context and tool surface, then measure it against document-retrieval baselines.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span class="maturity-flow">Governed inference deployment</span>
            <strong class="maturity-status">Current maturity · Implemented execution kernel, designed human gate</strong>
            <p><strong>Partnership work:</strong> assemble and validate the ITIP human gate, Norm and provenance evaluation, disposition audit, and regulated-estate proof.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span class="maturity-flow">Model specialisation</span>
            <strong class="maturity-status">Current maturity · Research hypothesis</strong>
            <p><strong>Partnership work:</strong> agree corpus permissions and oracle criteria, run specialisation experiments, and measure uplift.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span class="maturity-flow">Model evaluation and assurance</span>
            <strong class="maturity-status">Current maturity · Implemented primitives and integration proof</strong>
            <p><strong>Partnership work:</strong> define model evaluation contracts, datasets, baselines, trace capture, assurance criteria, and a repeatable service surface.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span class="maturity-flow">Model qualification and routing</span>
            <strong class="maturity-status">Current maturity · Implemented catalog and contracts</strong>
            <p><strong>Partnership work:</strong> implement routing, host bindings, workload evidence collection, model-version governance, and outcome-based qualification.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span class="maturity-flow">Agentic delivery</span>
            <strong class="maturity-status">Current maturity · Operational agent definitions, specified harness</strong>
            <p><strong>Partnership work:</strong> implement the harness runtime, bind partner models, collect controlled execution evidence, and establish repeatable outcome measures.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
        <div class="maturity-exchange">
          <span class="maturity-exchange-title">Cross-cutting operational adherence · Co-implementation</span>
          <p><strong>Direct value for Poesis:</strong> faster implementation, stronger experiments, benchmark evidence, and production feedback across the reference design.</p>
          <p><strong>Indirect value for the LLM vendor:</strong> a governed enterprise integration proving where its models perform, fail, and improve under accountable operating constraints.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>

<style is:global>
  .thesis-grid {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(6, 1fr); gap: 1rem; margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }
  .thesis-grid > .card { grid-column: span 2; }
  .thesis-grid > .card:nth-child(4) { grid-column: 2 / span 2; }

  .thesis-tagline {
    margin-top: .9rem; padding-top: .7rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    color: var(--accent-ink); font-weight: 700; font-size: .95rem;
  }
  .thesis-mechanisms {
    margin-top: .9rem; padding-top: .7rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: .8rem;
  }
  .thesis-mechanisms strong { color: var(--ink); }

  .reference-disclosure {
    max-width: 920px; margin-top: 1.2rem; padding: .8rem 1rem;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent); background: var(--accent-soft);
    color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: .9rem;
  }
  .reference-disclosure strong { color: var(--ink); }

  #vf .vf-mobile-flows { display: none; }

  .value-grid {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(6, 1fr); gap: 1rem; margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }
  .value-card {
    grid-column: span 2; width: 100%; color: inherit; font: inherit; text-align: left; cursor: pointer;
    transition: border-color .16s ease, box-shadow .16s ease, transform .16s ease;
  }
  .value-card:nth-child(7) { grid-column: 3 / span 2; }
  .value-card:hover, .value-card:focus-visible {
    border-color: var(--accent); box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px rgba(45, 212, 191, .14); transform: translateY(-2px); outline: none;
  }
  .value-card h3 { margin-top: .65rem; }
  .value-card p { min-height: 6.6rem; }
  .value-link { display: block; color: var(--accent-ink); font-size: .82rem; font-weight: 700; }

  .maturity-panel {
    margin: 0; padding: 0;
  }
  .maturity-panel h2 { max-width: 760px; margin-top: .4rem; }
  .maturity-panel > p:not(.eyebrow) { max-width: 860px; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .maturity-grid {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(6, 1fr); gap: .8rem; margin-top: 1.2rem;
  }
  .maturity-grid article {
    grid-column: span 2; padding: .85rem .95rem; border-left: 3px solid var(--line-strong);
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, .02);
  }
  .maturity-grid article:nth-child(7) { grid-column: 3 / span 2; }
  .maturity-grid p { margin: .45rem 0 0; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: .84rem; }
  .maturity-grid p strong { color: var(--ink); }
  .maturity-flow {
    display: block; color: var(--accent-ink); font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: .76rem; font-weight: 700;
  }
  .maturity-status { display: block; margin-top: .35rem; color: var(--ink); font-size: .88rem; }
  .maturity-exchange {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 1rem; margin-top: 1rem;
    padding: .9rem 1rem; border: 1px solid rgba(56, 189, 248, .4); border-radius: 8px;
    background: rgba(56, 189, 248, .08);
  }
  .maturity-exchange-title {
    grid-column: 1 / -1; color: var(--accent-ink); font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: .76rem; font-weight: 700;
  }
  .maturity-exchange p { margin: 0; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: .86rem; }
  .maturity-exchange strong { color: var(--ink); }

  #vf { margin-top: 1.5rem; }
  #vf .vf-notices { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: .75rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  #vf .vf-notice {
    margin: 0; border-radius: 10px; padding: .65rem .85rem; font-size: .86rem; color: var(--ink);
  }
  #vf .vf-notice-info { background: rgba(56, 189, 248, .08); border: 1px solid rgba(56, 189, 248, .4); }
  #vf .vf-notice-invariant { background: rgba(251, 191, 36, .10); border: 1px solid rgba(251, 191, 36, .45); }
  #vf .vf-human {
    border: 1px solid rgba(251, 146, 60, .5); background: rgba(251, 146, 60, .08); border-radius: 12px;
    padding: .75rem .9rem; margin: 0 0 1.2rem;
  }
  #vf .vf-human strong { color: #fb923c; }
  #vf .vf-human ul { margin: .45rem 0 0; padding-left: 1.2rem; font-size: .84rem; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  #vf .vf-human li { margin-top: .2rem; }

  #vf .vf-diagram { position: relative; }
  #vf #vf-wires { position: absolute; inset: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; pointer-events: none; z-index: 2; }
  #vf .vf-cols { position: relative; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 250px 1fr; z-index: 1; }
  #vf .vf-col { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1rem; }
  #vf .vf-gutter { pointer-events: none; }

  #vf .vf-group {
