    {
      id: 'D', hex: '#a78bfa', from: 'n-sie', to: 'n-train', lane: 0,
      label: 'governed material for model adaptation',
      title: 'D — Model adaptation & specialisation substrate (Poesis → LLM)',
      maturity: '<strong>Current maturity:</strong> research hypothesis. <strong>Partnership work:</strong> define adaptation tasks, corpus permissions, evaluation criteria, and baselines; then run controlled experiments and measure uplift.',
      sub: 'Governed Definitions and Ascription history could supply typed domain examples for continued pre-training, supervised fine-tuning, preference tuning, or distillation, but no corpus export or training integration exists. Mechanisms and Interactions encode modeled causal relations; lifecycle timestamps record temporal history, not causal proof. Human approvals and rejections are governance decisions, not automatically model-quality labels.',
      schema: [
